Z||000000||PaUL||04-07-99||06:49 PM||||Can anyone here tell me how to change the the control arm bushings? I read that you have to burn the old rubber ones out with a torch for the rears, but the upper fronts need to be pressed out. I found a site with lowest price for poly bushings: www.suspensons.com/fiero-prothane.htm<br> ....check it out, if anyone knows of place with lower prices let me know.
Z||000001||theogre||04-07-99||08:11 PM||||I've seen prothane's stuff, nice, haven't gotten any yet. Probably will soon. My SC is about due at 130Kmiles.<p>I asume you have the front bushings? If you don't wait till you get them. If they need pressing take then them to be done. DO NOT atempt to do it yourself. It must be done with a hydraulic press, and the work must be supported correctly or you will ruin the arm.<p>For any of the bushings that use old hardware, like the controlarms usually do. You must be very carefull not to damage the hardware. If you burn the bushings use care not to over heat the hardware. If you drill ir cut don't allow the drill/cutter in contect with the old hardware.<p>Rubber can be drilled, but it requires NEW, SHARP, bits, and constant lubrication.
Z||000002||PaUL||04-09-99||01:02 AM||||thanx  Ogre, do you have a fiero with poly bushing? if so did it improve the handling and is it worth getting?
